WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.325
Lifecycle Workflows carry joiner, mover
and leaver, so it helps to know the pieces.

2
00:00:05.325 --> 00:00:09.287
A workflow has a trigger, a
scope rule and a list of tasks.

3
00:00:09.287 --> 00:00:13.337
Custom task extensions call a
Logic App to reach other systems.

4
00:00:13.337 --> 00:00:18.101
Scheduled runs happen on one tenant
interval, every three hours by default.

5
00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:23.337
The limits are a hundred workflows, twenty-five
tasks each and a hundred extensions.

6
00:00:23.337 --> 00:00:25.750
Two behaviors deserve the red box.

7
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:30.593
Execution limits can quarantine a scheduled
run that would touch too many people,

8
00:00:30.593 --> 00:00:33.014
but an on-demand run skips that guardrail,

9
00:00:33.014 --> 00:00:35.863
and it ignores the workflow's
own conditions too.

10
00:00:35.863 --> 00:00:37.700
So what could break at our size?
